when he does.


00:30:54.210 --> 00:30:55.529
Come, come! Go, go, go!


00:30:55.610 --> 00:30:58.443
Rabbit, please, can we stop for lunch?


00:30:58.530 --> 00:31:01.727
Pooh, we cannot rest until
Christopher Robin is rescued.


00:31:01.810 --> 00:31:04.244
Try thinking of him instead of honey.


00:31:04.650 --> 00:31:08.086
- [rumbling]
- Very well. Christopher Robin.


00:31:08.170 --> 00:31:12.129
Christopher Robin. Christopher Robin!


00:31:12.810 --> 00:31:16.359
Ooh. It worked. Much better.


00:31:16.450 --> 00:31:18.600
[humming]


00:31:21.490 --> 00:31:22.718
[gasps]


00:31:26.730 --> 00:31:28.641
Does anybody see that?


00:31:28.730 --> 00:31:29.845
See what, honey?


00:31:29.930 --> 00:31:32.205
- Honey? Ooh!
- [rumbling]


00:31:32.290 --> 00:31:34.758
I can't wait to see the honey
on that Backson's honey


00:31:34.850 --> 00:31:37.239
when he falls into our honey. Eh, Owl?


00:31:37.330 --> 00:31:40.686
That cheeky honey will honey twice
before honeying our honey again.


00:31:40.770 --> 00:31:43.807
After we honey the honey,
can I honey a honey?


00:31:43.890 --> 00:31:46.404
Uh-uh-uh.
No honey before honey, honey.


00:31:46.490 --> 00:31:47.605
Wha... ?


00:31:47.690 --> 00:31:49.282
Honey up, Pooh. We have to honey.


00:31:49.370 --> 00:31:50.598
- [Owl] Honey.
- [Rabbit] Ooh, honey!


00:31:50.690 --> 00:31:51.679
- [Kanga] Yes.
- [Rabbit] Honey.


00:31:51.770 --> 00:31:54.204
[narrator] As Pooh watched
the honey honey away,


00:31:54.290 --> 00:31:56.042
his honey honey honey honey


00:31:56.130 --> 00:31:58.690
honey honey honey honey
honey honey honey...


00:31:58.770 --> 00:32:01.000
Ooh, Christopher Robin,
Christopher Robin,


00:32:01.090 --> 00:32:04.002
Christopher... hoo-hoo-hoo,
Christopher Robin.


