00:36:16.730 --> 00:36:17.879
Oh, this is lovely.


00:36:17.970 --> 00:36:22.486
We are stuck down here,
and the Backson is still up there.


00:36:22.570 --> 00:36:26.927
[whimpering] Oh, dear! Wait for me.


00:36:27.010 --> 00:36:28.762
No, Piglet! No, no, Piglet. Stay.


00:36:28.850 --> 00:36:31.045
But the Backson!


00:36:31.130 --> 00:36:33.598
You can help us if you stay up there!


00:36:33.690 --> 00:36:35.965
[straining]


00:36:36.690 --> 00:36:40.000
OK, Piglet, go look for something
to get us out of here.


00:36:40.090 --> 00:36:42.888
[stammering] OK.


00:36:42.970 --> 00:36:45.609
There might be
something over by the pack.


00:36:45.690 --> 00:36:47.681
Thank goodness one of us is up there.


00:36:47.770 --> 00:36:49.442
I was worried we'd be
stuck here forever.


00:36:49.530 --> 00:36:52.044
I found something. Here.


00:36:52.130 --> 00:36:53.199
- What?
- Ooh.


00:36:53.290 --> 00:36:55.565
That's a lovely flower, Piglet.


00:36:55.650 --> 00:36:57.527
Yeah, I thought so, too.


00:36:57.610 --> 00:37:00.602
Yes, Piglet,
it's very nice, a perennial.


00:37:00.690 --> 00:37:03.363
But I think we need something longer.


00:37:03.450 --> 00:37:08.001
Longer? Of course. How silly of me.


00:37:09.010 --> 00:37:10.284
[grunting]


00:37:12.970 --> 00:37:14.722
Oh, good thought, Piglet.


00:37:14.810 --> 00:37:17.563
But you can't possibly think
that that's long enough.


00:37:17.650 --> 00:37:20.767
Oh, yes, it is.
Owl read this to me once,


00:37:20.850 --> 00:37:24.047
and it was certainly the longest thing
I'd ever heard.


00:37:24.130 --> 00:37:25.119
[giggles] Oh.


00:37:25.210 --> 00:37:28.441
It's true, Rabbit.
It lags a bit in the middle.


00:37:28.530 --> 00:37:31.806
Of all things, why didn't we think
to bring a rope?


00:37:31.890 --> 00:37:34.324
Well, there is this rope.


00:37:36.130 --> 00:37:40.203
Spot-on, Piglet. Do be a helpful
little swine and get us out of here.


00:37:40.290 --> 00:37:41.484
All of you?


00:37:41.570 --> 00:37:44.004
Yes, Piglet, all of us.


00:37:44.770 --> 00:37:48.285
All right. Three, four...
Don't forget Rabbit.


00:37:51.450 --> 00:37:53.406
[scissors snipping]


00:37:54.890 --> 00:37:56.642
[Piglet] And six.


00:37:56.730 --> 00:37:59.039
There! Now you can all get out!


00:37:59.130 --> 00:38:02.122
How very thoughtful you are, Piglet.


00:38:02.210 --> 00:38:05.043
Good grief! Tie them together, Piglet.


00:38:05.130 --> 00:38:06.882
Can you tie a knot?


00:38:06.970 --> 00:38:08.005
I cannot.


00:38:08.090 --> 00:38:09.489
So, you can knot.


00:38:09.570 --> 00:38:11.401
No, I cannot knot.


00:38:11.490 --> 00:38:13.560
- Not knot?
- Who's there?


00:38:13.650 --> 00:38:14.719
- Pooh!
- Pooh who?


00:38:14.810 --> 00:38:16.289
No! Pooh, it's...


00:38:16.370 --> 00:38:18.930
Piglet, you'll need more than two knots.


00:38:19.010 --> 00:38:20.125
Not possible.


00:38:20.210 --> 00:38:23.441
Ah! So, it is possible
to knot those pieces.


00:38:23.530 --> 00:38:24.599
Not these pieces.


00:38:24.690 --> 00:38:26.646
Yes, knot those pieces.


00:38:26.730 --> 00:38:29.244
- Why not?
- Because it's all for naught.


00:38:29.330 --> 00:38:32.925
Oh, dear! I can't tie a knot.


00:38:33.010 --> 00:38:34.887
But there is something I can do.


00:38:36.090 --> 00:38:39.560
Don't worry, Rabbit.
Piglet's very clever.


00:38:39.650 --> 00:38:41.720
I can tie a bow.


00:38:41.810 --> 00:38:43.482
- See?
- [groans]


00:38:43.570 --> 00:38:46.482
For crying out loud! Piglet!


00:38:46.570 --> 00:38:48.800
I know! Christopher Robin
has a jump rope.


00:38:48.890 --> 00:38:50.118
Ahh!


00:38:50.210 --> 00:38:53.441
Wait a minute. My gracious, that's it!


00:38:53.530 --> 00:38:56.567
Piglet, go to Christopher Robin's house.


00:38:56.650 --> 00:38:57.878
Oh, I see.


00:38:57.970 --> 00:39:00.768
Yes, Piglet, go, and bring some honey.


00:39:00.850 --> 00:39:02.249
Yes, bring some honey...


00:39:02.330 --> 00:39:04.924
[gasps] The jump rope,
Piglet, the jump rope.


00:39:05.010 --> 00:39:07.399
With a little honey on the side.


00:39:07.490 --> 00:39:10.209
You mean, all by myself?


00:39:13.170 --> 00:39:15.320
Through there?


00:39:15.410 --> 00:39:16.889
Yes, Piglet.


00:39:17.890 --> 00:39:20.768
Through a dark wood fraught with peril,


00:39:20.850 --> 00:39:22.681
on a mission of life or death.


00:39:22.770 --> 00:39:25.489
It is a task of great complexity,


00:39:25.570 --> 00:39:29.688
but I have full confidence
that you shall return victorious,


00:39:29.770 --> 00:39:32.523
and rescue us from the abyss.


00:39:32.610 --> 00:39:35.443
Go forth, Piglet,
and we shall await your return.


00:39:35.530 --> 00:39:37.919
For weeks, if necessary.


00:39:41.250 --> 00:39:42.524
Owl!


00:39:45.650 --> 00:39:46.765
What?


00:39:46.850 --> 00:39:51.241
I can't believe how wonderful
that speech was.


00:39:51.330 --> 00:39:52.604
I can't, either.


00:39:52.690 --> 00:39:54.681
Moved me to tears.


00:39:55.490 --> 00:39:59.529
[narrator] So Piglet bravely ventured
forth towards Christopher Robin's house.


00:39:59.610 --> 00:40:04.400
But the further he went,
the more frightened he became.


00:40:04.490 --> 00:40:07.402
[whimpering] Oh, dear.


00:40:08.130 --> 00:40:10.200
I mustn't fear.


00:40:11.570 --> 00:40:15.165
There's a very important thing to...


00:40:15.250 --> 00:40:18.959
[heavy stammer] Do...


00:40:19.050 --> 00:40:20.608
[screams]


00:40:20.690 --> 00:40:23.045
[whimpering]


00:40:25.650 --> 00:40:30.326
Oh. It's just you, B'loon.
I'll get some help.


00:40:31.050 --> 00:40:33.405
Oh, dear. I am the help.


00:40:35.810 --> 00:40:38.085
How did you ever get stuck up there?


00:40:38.170 --> 00:40:41.128
It wasn't the Backson, was it?


00:40:42.770 --> 00:40:43.998
Oh, good.


00:40:44.090 --> 00:40:46.126
I knew the Backson wasn't around here.


00:40:46.210 --> 00:40:47.962
[grunts]


00:40:56.570 --> 00:40:57.844
[Tigger grunts]


00:40:57.930 --> 00:41:00.000
[moaning]


00:41:00.090 --> 00:41:02.604
[stammering] Backson!


00:41:02.690 --> 00:41:04.601
Huh?! Backson?


00:41:06.170 --> 00:41:08.365
- [screaming]
- Piglet, help!


00:41:10.370 --> 00:41:11.598
Whew.


00:41:11.690 --> 00:41:13.328
[shouting]


00:41:22.210 --> 00:41:25.646
Let me tell you, that was the last time
I'll ever put my beak


00:41:25.730 --> 00:41:27.402
- in a keyhole.
- Shh-shh-shh!


00:41:27.490 --> 00:41:29.879
[whispers] Do you hear something?


00:41:30.970 --> 00:41:32.961
- Help! Help me!
- Piglet!


00:41:33.050 --> 00:41:35.041
He knows my name!


00:41:36.450 --> 00:41:37.963
[blowing hard]


00:41:40.210 --> 00:41:41.768
- Yeah!
- [gasp]


00:41:42.850 --> 00:41:44.363
Whoa! Oh!


00:41:44.450 --> 00:41:46.042
[shouting]


00:41:52.090 --> 00:41:53.489
Ah!


00:41:55.330 --> 00:41:57.719
- [straining]
- [grunting]


00:42:02.130 --> 00:42:03.609
[groaning]


00:42:03.690 --> 00:42:05.442
[screams]


00:42:07.250 --> 00:42:08.842
[Piglet groans]


00:42:09.530 --> 00:42:10.645
[all gasp] Backson!


00:42:11.810 --> 00:42:13.880
Whew! It's only Tigger.


00:42:13.970 --> 00:42:17.007
Oh! Hi, fellas!


00:42:17.090 --> 00:42:20.878
Tigger Two?
I thought the Backson got you.


00:42:20.970 --> 00:42:22.801
Ahh. As soon as we get out of here,


00:42:22.890 --> 00:42:26.280
we're gonna show that Backson
what Tiggers are made of, aren't we?


00:42:26.370 --> 00:42:29.123
Thanks, but I'd rather stay an Eeyore.


00:42:29.210 --> 00:42:32.088
What? But what about all the pouncing
and the trouncing?


00:42:32.170 --> 00:42:34.809
And the mixing it up?
I thought you liked being a Tigger.


00:42:34.890 --> 00:42:37.404
The most wonderful thing about Tiggers,


00:42:37.490 --> 00:42:40.323
is you're the only one.


00:42:40.410 --> 00:42:44.164
Aw, shucks. I'm speechless.


00:42:44.250 --> 00:42:45.478
[Piglet] Excuse me.


00:42:45.570 --> 00:42:49.085
- I can't breathe! [groans]
- [Tigger] Oh.


00:42:51.810 --> 00:42:55.598
Sorry about that, little guy.
I didn't mean to scare you.


00:42:55.690 --> 00:42:57.885
Wait! B'loon! Don't leave!


00:42:58.930 --> 00:43:01.239
[Piglet] You're the only one
who can get us out of here!


00:43:01.330 --> 00:43:04.049
We're all gonna die.


00:43:04.890 --> 00:43:07.120
Cheer up, Eeyore.
We won't perish for days.


00:43:07.210 --> 00:43:10.008
Which leaves plenty of time for me
to continue my memoirs.


00:43:10.090 --> 00:43:11.489
Now, dear Uncle Ridley...


00:43:11.570 --> 00:43:12.969
♪ Honey ♪


00:43:13.050 --> 00:43:14.722
[Owl] ...exacerbated
by my aunt's predilection


00:43:14.810 --> 00:43:17.005
- for only the finest parchment...
- Hmm. [gasps]


00:43:17.090 --> 00:43:19.604
...woven so tightly
the ink took weeks to fully dry.


00:43:19.690 --> 00:43:22.602
Their nest was littered with quills
that were never used,


00:43:22.690 --> 00:43:25.158
papers that were never cut,
and letters that never dried.


00:43:25.250 --> 00:43:28.959
My aunt often bemoaned the situation in
letters that she couldn't write to me.


00:43:29.050 --> 00:43:31.769
It drove my poor uncle absolutely batty,


00:43:31.850 --> 00:43:34.364
which is quite a feat for an owl,
I assure you.


00:43:34.450 --> 00:43:37.601
Now, when my uncle had committed
an exceedingly rousing point...


00:43:37.690 --> 00:43:38.839
Empty.


00:43:40.010 --> 00:43:42.649
...and let me tell you,
it packed quite a wallop.


00:43:42.730 --> 00:43:44.243
- [groans]
- Huh?


00:43:44.330 --> 00:43:45.524
Look! Look, the letters!


00:43:45.610 --> 00:43:47.885
The ladder! The ladders formed a letter!


00:43:47.970 --> 00:43:49.961
I mean the letters... We can get out!


00:43:50.050 --> 00:43:54.566
[narrator] And so they all used the
letter ladder to climb out of the pit.


00:43:55.530 --> 00:43:58.602
But little did they know that
coming through the bushes was...


00:43:58.690 --> 00:44:00.840
- [branches snapping]
- [all gasp] Backson!


00:44:00.930 --> 00:44:02.329
Back to the pit!


00:44:02.410 --> 00:44:04.605
[Christopher] Wait, everyone.


00:44:05.210 --> 00:44:07.087
It's only me.


00:44:07.170 --> 00:44:09.365
[all] Christopher Robin!


00:44:10.530 --> 00:44:12.725
You found them, B'loon. Well done.


00:44:12.810 --> 00:44:15.483
It's Christopher Robin!


00:44:15.570 --> 00:44:17.640
How did you escape from the Backson?


00:44:17.730 --> 00:44:20.528
Backson? What on earth is a Backson?


00:44:20.610 --> 00:44:21.804
He wakes up babies!


00:44:21.890 --> 00:44:23.209
He swipes your stripes!


00:44:23.290 --> 00:44:24.769
He puts out the lights!


00:44:24.850 --> 00:44:28.240
Yes, and we thought he took you from us.


00:44:28.330 --> 00:44:31.800
What gave you the idea
I was taken by a Backson?


00:44:31.890 --> 00:44:33.448
Your note.


00:44:34.730 --> 00:44:39.246
[narrator] Christopher Robin explained
that it had all been a misunderstanding.


00:44:39.330 --> 00:44:42.083
And now that it was autumn,
the school year had begun.


00:44:42.170 --> 00:44:47.085
His note was simply to say he had
gone out and would be back soon.


00:44:48.370 --> 00:44:50.520
[all] Oh!


00:44:52.730 --> 00:44:54.243
Ooh. Um...


00:44:56.930 --> 00:44:58.921
OK.


00:44:59.010 --> 00:45:01.319
It's getting late.
We ought to be heading back.


00:45:01.410 --> 00:45:02.530
Just a moment, everyone.


00:45:02.530 --> 00:45:03.121
Just a moment, everyone.


00:45:03.210 --> 00:45:04.928
Oh, yes. You're right, Piglet.


00:45:05.010 --> 00:45:07.001
We owe a very special someone...


00:45:07.090 --> 00:45:10.207
...a token of our appreciation.


00:45:10.290 --> 00:45:11.439
Ohh!


00:45:11.530 --> 00:45:15.364
This reward goes to a good friend
and a loyal companion.


00:45:15.450 --> 00:45:17.725
Someone who not only helped us
out of this pit,


00:45:17.810 --> 00:45:20.040
but also found Christopher Robin.


00:45:20.130 --> 00:45:23.918
And he just so happens
to be wearing red today.


00:45:24.010 --> 00:45:26.968
So it is with great, great honour
and a humble heart,


00:45:27.050 --> 00:45:31.123
that I bestow this pot of honey
upon our dear friend...


00:45:31.210 --> 00:45:32.404
...B'loon.


00:45:32.490 --> 00:45:33.889
Wonderful idea, Rabbit.


00:45:33.970 --> 00:45:36.359
- Hooray!
- Hooray, B'loon!


00:45:36.930 --> 00:45:40.240
- Thank you, B'loon. Goodbye.
- Hooray!


00:45:40.330 --> 00:45:44.289
[narrator] Pooh watched as B'loon took
the honey pot higher and higher,


00:45:44.370 --> 00:45:48.966
until it was completely out of sight.


00:45:49.050 --> 00:45:51.689
Oh, bother.


00:45:57.570 --> 00:45:59.720
Sorry, Pooh.


00:45:59.810 --> 00:46:04.440
Ever have one of those days
where you just can't win, Eeyore?


00:46:04.530 --> 00:46:08.000
Yep. I know how you feel.


00:46:12.090 --> 00:46:14.206
- [rumbling]
- Oh, yes.


00:46:14.290 --> 00:46:16.485
I simply must find some honey.


00:46:16.570 --> 00:46:19.607
[narrator] As Pooh continued searching,
he got hungrier...


00:46:20.810 --> 00:46:22.960
- Oh!
- ...and hungrier...


00:46:23.730 --> 00:46:26.688
- Yes, tummy, I know.
- ...and hungrier...


00:46:26.770 --> 00:46:28.601
Ohh...


00:46:28.690 --> 00:46:32.126
...until he found himself
at Owl's house.


00:46:46.050 --> 00:46:47.039
[bell jingles]


00:46:49.130 --> 00:46:51.769
Well, stone the crows.
If it isn't Pooh Bear.


00:46:51.850 --> 00:46:54.045
Hello, Owl.


00:46:54.130 --> 00:46:57.088
Well, congratulate me.


00:46:57.170 --> 00:46:59.730
- For what?
- I have achieved completion


00:46:59.810 --> 00:47:02.688
of my autobiographical treatise!


00:47:02.770 --> 00:47:04.442
Oh! Was it painful?


00:47:04.530 --> 00:47:07.567
No, no, no. My memoirs are finished.


00:47:07.650 --> 00:47:08.844
Oh.


00:47:09.370 --> 00:47:12.965
Dash it all, Pooh. Why do you keep
staring at that bell rope?


00:47:13.050 --> 00:47:17.646
Because it reminds me of something.


00:47:17.730 --> 00:47:20.369
And that reminds me
of another something.


00:47:20.450 --> 00:47:22.361
Perhaps I could borrow some honey?


00:47:22.450 --> 00:47:26.125
Just a taste? A drop, perhaps?


00:47:26.210 --> 00:47:27.802
A small lick, I should think.


00:47:27.890 --> 00:47:30.768
My boy, I shall do better than that.


00:47:30.850 --> 00:47:32.761
Not only will I beckon you to my table,


00:47:32.850 --> 00:47:36.604
but as we feast,
I shall treat you to an excerpt


00:47:36.690 --> 00:47:38.965
from chapter 127,


00:47:39.050 --> 00:47:43.248
which tells the gripping tale of how
only a few days ago,


00:47:43.330 --> 00:47:46.367
I found that very handsome bell rope
that you were admiring


00:47:46.450 --> 00:47:49.681
just hanging over a thistle bush.


00:47:49.770 --> 00:47:51.044
Thistle bush?


00:47:51.130 --> 00:47:52.848
Or was it a gorse bush?


00:47:52.930 --> 00:47:56.002
No. No. It was definitely
a thistle bush.


00:47:56.090 --> 00:47:57.284
Pardon me, Owl.


00:47:57.370 --> 00:47:59.930
At first I thought someone lived there,
so I rang it.


00:48:00.010 --> 00:48:01.204
No one answered.


00:48:01.290 --> 00:48:04.043
And then the thing just fell off
in my hand.


00:48:04.130 --> 00:48:07.964
What sort of place
was this particular thistle bush in?


00:48:08.050 --> 00:48:10.245
Certainly not a very cheery place.


00:48:10.330 --> 00:48:12.400
One might say it was rather...


00:48:12.490 --> 00:48:13.889
Gloomy?


00:48:13.970 --> 00:48:16.438
Yes. That's it. Do you know it?


00:48:16.530 --> 00:48:17.758
Oh, dear.


00:48:17.850 --> 00:48:20.364
Nobody seemed to want it,
so I brought it home.


00:48:20.450 --> 00:48:23.044
Oh, but somebody did want it, Owl.


00:48:23.130 --> 00:48:24.483
Really? Who?


00:48:24.570 --> 00:48:27.482
Eeyore. My dear friend Eeyore.


00:48:27.570 --> 00:48:29.481
He was fond of it, you see.


00:48:29.570 --> 00:48:32.130
- Fond of it?
- Attached to it.


00:48:32.210 --> 00:48:33.768
Attached?


00:48:33.850 --> 00:48:35.647
Ohh!


00:48:35.730 --> 00:48:37.641
Yes. Well, yes.


00:48:37.730 --> 00:48:41.484
And I was just keeping it safe for him.


00:48:41.570 --> 00:48:44.642
Well, there you are.
And you can tell him he's welcome.


00:48:44.730 --> 00:48:47.688
Yes, Owl. And thank you very much.


00:48:47.770 --> 00:48:50.648
I say, Pooh! What about the honey?


00:48:54.010 --> 00:48:56.001
[tummy rumbles]


00:48:57.250 --> 00:48:59.639
Some other time, perhaps?


00:49:01.530 --> 00:49:04.090
[narrator] Ignoring his tummy's
desperate pleas,


00:49:04.170 --> 00:49:06.286
Pooh went directly
to Christopher Robin's.


00:49:06.370 --> 00:49:07.359
Tail.


00:49:08.170 --> 00:49:09.922
Nail.


00:49:10.010 --> 00:49:11.159
Hammer.


00:49:14.970 --> 00:49:16.961
So what do you think, Eeyore?


00:49:17.050 --> 00:49:19.120
I'll test it out.


00:49:20.690 --> 00:49:22.920
Seems about the right length.


00:49:23.010 --> 00:49:25.524
Pink bow's a nice touch.


00:49:26.490 --> 00:49:29.800
Swishes real good, too.


00:49:29.890 --> 00:49:32.006
So, are you happy, Eeyore?


00:49:32.090 --> 00:49:34.160
- No.
- Ooh.


00:49:34.250 --> 00:49:37.526
But I sure do like this new tail.


00:49:39.410 --> 00:49:40.889
Thank you, Pooh.


00:49:41.810 --> 00:49:44.529
And now,
I have a surprise for you, Pooh.


00:49:44.610 --> 00:49:47.078
I do like surprises.


00:49:47.170 --> 00:49:49.445
[Christopher] OK. Open your eyes.


00:49:49.530 --> 00:49:51.407
They're open, Christopher.


00:49:51.490 --> 00:49:54.766
[Christopher] No, silly.
Put your arms down.


00:49:56.050 --> 00:50:00.521
Congratulations, Pooh.
You win the grand prize!


00:50:00.610 --> 00:50:03.522
♪ It's Pooh
It's Pooh


00:50:03.610 --> 00:50:06.078
♪ Pooh wins the honey pot


00:50:06.170 --> 00:50:08.923
♪ You're the winner of the prize


00:50:09.010 --> 00:50:11.444
♪ I really can't believe my eyes


00:50:11.530 --> 00:50:14.363
♪ Pooh gets the honey


00:50:14.450 --> 00:50:16.839
♪ Honey, honey, honey, honey


00:50:16.930 --> 00:50:18.158
Here you go, Pooh.


00:50:18.250 --> 00:50:20.002
Oh, yes, of course.


00:50:26.690 --> 00:50:29.443
- [all gasp]
- Thank you all ever so much.


00:50:30.370 --> 00:50:34.079
♪ Everything is honey
Everything is good


00:50:34.170 --> 00:50:38.163
♪ Everyone is happy
in the Hundred Acre Wood


00:50:38.250 --> 00:50:41.447
♪ A honey happy ending
for a Pooh to eat


00:50:41.530 --> 00:50:45.887
♪ Yes, everything is honey


00:50:45.970 --> 00:50:51.966
♪ And life is very sweet ♪


00:50:52.090 --> 00:50:55.480
You know, Pooh, you did
a very important thing today.


00:50:55.570 --> 00:50:58.323
- I did?
- Well, yes.


00:50:58.410 --> 00:51:01.641
Instead of thinking of your tummy,
you thought of your friend.


00:51:01.730 --> 00:51:03.368
Oh, thank you, Christopher Robin.


00:51:03.450 --> 00:51:06.840
And now I don't think
I shall be hungry again


00:51:06.930 --> 00:51:09.842
for a good long while.


00:51:09.930 --> 00:51:12.319
- [tummy rumbles]
- [Pooh] Oh, bother.


00:51:12.410 --> 00:51:14.082
[Christopher] Silly old bear.


00:57:00.050 --> 00:57:01.244
[sighs]


00:57:10.570 --> 00:57:11.969
[croaks]


00:57:59.770 --> 00:58:01.761
Oh! Ooh, ooh, ooh!


00:58:23.970 --> 00:58:26.962
[unintelligible dialogue]


00:59:26.570 --> 00:59:29.403
- [crickets chirring]
- [frogs croaking]


00:59:30.810 --> 00:59:32.209
[thudding]


00:59:40.810 --> 00:59:44.359
Wow! It's amazing
what you can find in the woods.


00:59:44.450 --> 00:59:47.442
A marble! And a boot!


00:59:47.530 --> 00:59:51.239
And oh, my,
that's a scary-lookin' fella.


00:59:51.330 --> 00:59:54.288
Gosh! Maybe these are his things.


00:59:54.370 --> 00:59:56.964
You know, I better pick 'em up
so they won't get broken.


00:59:57.050 --> 00:59:58.642
That's the last thing I would want.


00:59:58.730 --> 01:00:00.049
Whoa!


01:00:00.530 --> 01:00:03.363
- [thud]
- [grunt] Oh, my gosh!


01:00:03.450 --> 01:00:06.567
Is this a pit? I think I'm in a pit!


01:00:06.650 --> 01:00:09.767
Hello? Anybody up there?


01:00:09.850 --> 01:00:14.048
Oh, well. I sure hope that fella
will be back soon.

